Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

harness-6l restructures the original skill around the six-layer harness
architecture (guides, sensors, agentic loop, memory, permissions,
observability). The following files are derivative works of the original
and have been changed; each carries a notice at the end of the file.

  skills/harness/SKILL.md
      Derived from the original SKILL.md. Rewritten around a five-stage
      workflow and a decision filter. Trigger phrases, the operations
      workflow, agent/skill duplication review, follow-up-work support,
      and the deliverables checklist are retained from the original.

  skills/harness/references/multi-agent.md
      Merged and revised from references/agent-design-patterns.md,
      references/orchestrator-template.md and references/team-examples.md.

  skills/harness/references/skill-authoring.md
      Merged and revised from references/skill-writing-guide.md and
      references/skill-testing-guide.md.

  skills/harness/references/verifier-agent.md
  skills/harness/references/verifier-web-checklist.md
      Revised from references/qa-agent-guide.md. The web-specific
      boundary checklist was split into its own file in 1.1.0.

  skills/harness/references/ratchet.md
      The operations/maintenance procedure and the evolution triggers are
      derived from the original SKILL.md Phase 7.

Substantive behavioural changes from the original:

  * The unconditional `model: "opus"` requirement is withdrawn. Agents now
    default to the smallest model that fits the task; only the explicitness
    of the `model` parameter is retained.
  * Verifier agents no longer receive write access. A verifier reports
    failures and does not rewrite the artifact it judges.
  * Permission boundaries, capability budgets, structured logging and trip
    wires are added. Every budget line must declare `enforced_by`.
  * `AGENTS.md` is not produced. Claude Code loads `CLAUDE.md`, not
    `AGENTS.md`, so `CLAUDE.md` is the guide file.
  * Checkpoints expire: one per active task, overwrite-as-expiry.

The following files are original works of harness-6l and are not derived
from the upstream project:

  skills/harness/references/layers.md
  skills/harness/references/enforcement.md
  skills/harness/assets/**   (hooks: _common.sh, policy_gate.sh, loop_budget.sh,
                              audit_log.sh, test_gate.sh — test_gate.sh was first
                              drafted during the 1.1.0 adversarial usage simulation)
  skills/harness/evals/trigger_eval.json
  scripts/check.sh

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Conceptual sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The six-layer architecture, the ratchet principle, the guides-and-sensors
taxonomy and the control-reliability ladder are drawn from publicly
published engineering writing, in particular:

  * Mitchell Hashimoto — "My AI Adoption Journey" (ratchet principle,
    one rule per failure)
  * Birgitta Boeckeler / Martin Fowler — guides-and-sensors taxonomy
  * OpenAI Codex engineering field reports (guide file as system of record,
    compaction)
  * LangChain engineering — agent harness anatomy
  * Lauren Tan / Cursor — converting repeated review comments into
    structural constraints

These are cited as sources of ideas. No text from them is reproduced here.
